# State and persistence

Use mock database services backed by `SharedPreferences`. All CRUD must work, stay reactive, and survive app restarts for the live viva.

## Rules

- Put mock services in `lib/core/` (or a feature `data/` folder that writes through the mock DB).
- Every create/update/delete must persist immediately, then notify listeners (`ChangeNotifier` / `Provider`).
- Do not use in-memory-only lists as the source of truth.
- Seed once if storage is empty; never wipe user data on hot restart.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
final courts = <Court>[]; // lost on restart

// ✅ GOOD
class MockDatabase extends ChangeNotifier {
  Future<void> upsertCourt(Court court) async {
    // write JSON to SharedPreferences, then notifyListeners()
  }
}
```
